      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482286395": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nQuora operates in the knowledge sharing and artificial intelligence space, addressing the challenge of organizing and distributing collective intelligence on a global scale. The organization provides two main platforms: a knowledge sharing site with millions of monthly users, and a cloud workspace for running AI agents collaboratively. This setup supports a wide user base and integrates multiple AI models, highlighting the company's emphasis on leveraging machine learning to enhance information access and collaboration.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER NEW GRAD, MACHINE LEARNING PLATFORM role focuses on developing and maintaining the infrastructure that supports large-scale machine learning models. This position contributes directly to the reliability, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems that serve hundreds of millions of users, enabling machine learning engineers to work more effectively. The role offers hands-on experience with distributed systems, GPU serving, and ML platform modernization, impacting the long-term success of the organization's core products.\nResponsibilities:\nBuild and maintain core infrastructure for the machine learning platform ensuring availability and scalability\nDevelop distributed systems for serving diverse machine learning models in production\nOptimize GPU model serving to improve latency, throughput, and cost efficiency\nContribute to platform standardization and modernization efforts\nCreate tools to enhance machine learning engineer productivity\nModernize feature store for faster feature deployment\nParticipate in on-call rotations to manage production issues\nRequirements:\nAvailability during coordination hours (Monday to Friday, 9am to 3pm Pacific Time)\nExpected 2025 or 2026 graduate in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field\nInterest in large-scale distributed systems and machine learning infrastructure\nFamiliarity or ability to learn Python, Go, or C++\nCommitment to continuous learning and team improvement\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nFor US-based applicants, the salary is $97,600\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical insurance\nVision insurance\nDental insurance\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482289320": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the software engineering sector, focusing on developing internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. It addresses the challenge of creating scalable, reliable software systems that enhance internal processes and productivity. The company is positioned to impact the engineering and operational efficiency through innovative platform capabilities.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER, NEW GRAD role is designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers aiming to accelerate their professional growth by building production software systems. This position involves contributing to and eventually owning core internal platform capabilities and product features. The role is critical in supporting internal workflows and platforms, ensuring the delivery of reliable, maintainable, and scalable software solutions.\nResponsibilities:\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems supporting critical internal workflows and platforms.\nBuild maintainable backend services and APIs following scalable engineering practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces for internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate concepts into production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvements.\nAssist in troubleshooting production issues to build resilient and observable systems.\nDevelop engineering judgment to balance speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or related field (recent graduate or soon to graduate).\nExperience through internships, co-ops, research, or personal projects in software application development.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and data modeling principles.\nKnowledge of RESTful APIs and distributed application communication.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nMotivation to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-paced engineering environment.\nPreferred:\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483110281": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nAbout Perseus Payments Inc.\nPerseus Payments Inc., part of Constellation Software, builds PerseusPay. PerseusPay is a cloud-native payments platform for marine, outdoor power equipment and RV dealers in the US and Canada. The platform is PCI DSS compliant, and the team is building toward an AI-native way of developing software.\nWhy This Role\nThis is a chance to build features on a live payments platform used by hundreds of dealer locations. You will own work from an incomplete brief through to production, across backend, UI and payment processor integrations. The platform is secure, PCI-compliant and built to scale.\nRole Overview\nWe are hiring a software developer for the team that builds new PerseusPay features, as distinct from our support and platform work. You will own features from an incomplete brief through to production: shaping the design, building the backend APIs and UI, working through payment-processor rules, and shipping behind feature flags. Requirements on a payments product change often, because processor behaviour, compliance rules, DMS partner needs and dealer feedback all move. We want someone who finds that interesting and keeps delivering without waiting to be told what to do next.\nKey Responsibilities\nTake a feature from PRD or user story to production: clarify the scope, design the solution, build, test, and release behind a feature flag.\nBuild and maintain REST APIs, background processing and database changes in C# / .NET.\nBuild and maintain React UI for the dealer portal, the embedded payment page and the checkout plugin.\nIntegrate with payment processor APIs and webhooks, and read processor documentation to find the edge cases that matter.\nSpot gaps, contradictions and missing edge cases in requirements, and bring them to the Product Owner and Director of R&D with a recommended option.\nRe-plan quickly when scope changes, and say clearly what that does to the delivery date.\nWrite unit and integration tests, take part in code reviews, and meet our SonarQube and secure coding standards.\nKeep production safe with structured logging, error handling, idempotency, retries and concurrency safety on money-moving flows.\nSupport QA with test data and fixes, and support release validation.\nKeep technical notes, decision records and Azure DevOps items current so work is traceable.\nWork with the team’s AI-assisted and agentic development tools, including Claude Code, within our security rules.\nOur Tech Stack\nBackend: C# on .NET 8 (moving toward .NET 10), ASP.NET Core Web API, Entity Framework Core, Azure Functions.\nFrontend: React / JavaScript SPA.\nData: Azure SQL (SQL Server), Redis, Azure Service Bus.\nAzure: App Service, API Management, Front Door with WAF, Functions, SignalR, Key Vault, App Configuration, Application Insights.\nSecurity and identity: OAuth2 / JWT, Duende IdentityServer, PCI DSS v4.0.1 controls, SonarQube SAST.\nDelivery and observability: Azure DevOps (boards, repos, YAML pipelines), Datadog, feature flags, Postman.\nAI-assisted and agentic development: Claude Code, Claude-based code review and test generation, and project context files and skills shared across the team.\nRequired Skills & Experience\n5+ years of professional software development, with strong C#/ .NET and ASP.NET Core REST API experience.\nStrong SQL Server skills: schema design, query tuning, transactions, and an understanding of locking and deadlocks.\nHands-on Azure experience: App Services, Functions, Service Bus, Application Insights.\nReact / JavaScript working knowledge, enough to ship UI features independently.\nA proven record of delivering features with incomplete or changing requirements. Be ready to give examples in the interview.\nAbility to work independently across time zones. You make sound decisions, record them, and escalate with a recommendation rather than a question.\nStrong written English. Most of our collaboration is written, in Azure DevOps, pull requests and Teams.\nSolid engineering habits: unit tests, code reviews, Git branching, CI/CD.\nFamiliarity with Agile/Scrum and Azure DevOps.\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering or a related field, or equivalent experience.\nPreferred Skills (Nice-to-Have)\nHands-on experience with Claude Code or a comparable agentic coding tool, and knowledge of agentic engineering practices: spec-driven development, context engineering, task decomposition, test-driven feedback loops, and critical review of agent output.\nYou should be able to describe a feature you shipped this way, including where the agent went wrong.\nExperience with MCP servers, custom skills or sub-agents, multi-agent workflows, and evals for AI-generated code.\nPayment processor integration experience.\nRedis caching and Service Bus patterns.\nDatadog, Azure DevOps pipelines, Terraform awareness.\nAbout You\nYou are self-directed. You do not wait for a perfect spec or a daily check-in.\nYou are comfortable with unknowns and expect requirements to change. You ask the sharp question early, usually about an edge case or a rule nobody has written down yet.\nYou take ownership of outcomes, not just tickets. You think about what happens in production and for the dealer.\nYou communicate proactively through short, clear written updates, flagged risks and visible progress.\nYou hold the quality bar when money is involved. You treat security, idempotency and auditability as part of the feature.\nYou are curious, learn fast, and are open to AI-assisted development. You use it to raise your output without lowering your standards.\nExciting Benefits We Offer\nMarket-leading Salary\nMedical Coverage – Self & Dependents\nParents Medical Coverage\nProvident Fund\nEmployee Performance-based bonuses\nHome Internet Subsidy\nConveyance Allowance\nProfit Sharing Plan [Tenured Employees Only]\nLife Benefit\nChild Care Facility\nCompany Provided Lunch/Dinner\nProfessional Development Budget\nRecreational area for in-house games\nSporadic On-shore training opportunities\nFriendly work environment\nLeave Encashment\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483166364": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Posting Details\nJob Title Application Programmer Analyst I\nRequisition Number RE56239\nWorking Title\nDepartment Name 7P275:Public Health Analytics and Informatics\nWork Location Lexington, KY\nGrade Level 46\nSalary Range $53,061-87,526/year\nType of Position Staff\nPosition Time Status Full-Time\nRequired Education\nBS\nClick here for more information about equivalencies: https://hr.uky.edu/employment/working-uk/equivalencies\nRequired Related Experience\n1 yr\nRequired License/Registration/Certification\nNone\nPhysical Requirements\nSitting and/or standing for long periods of time; performing repetitive motion tasks; lifting, pushing, and/or pulling objects up to 50lbs\nShift\nMonday – Friday Between the hours of 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. Additional hours as needed\nJob Summary\nBuild Technology Solutions That Support Public Health Across Kentucky\nThe University of Kentucky is seeking an Application Programmer Analyst I to join theCollege of Public Health’s Public Health Analytics and Informatics team .\nThis position develops and maintains applications supporting state-funded public health projects, including the DBHDID contract with the State of Kentucky. Working with principal investigators, technical team members, and contract stakeholders, this role contributes throughout the Software Development Life Cycle ( SDLC ) to deliver reliable solutions that meet project and stakeholder needs.\nWhat You’ll Do\nDevelop, test, debug, deploy, and maintain web-based applications and databases using established development standards.\nBuild solutions using technologies such as C#, ASP . NET Core, MVC , Web Forms, HTML , CSS , Less, JavaScript, TypeScript, jQuery, T- SQL , Power Platform, Azure App Service, Azure Functions, and SQL Server.\nDevelop and maintain contract-specific applications and databases supporting analytical needs in public health, behavioral health, and intellectual disabilities.\nEvaluate project needs, analyze requirements, prepare workflow documentation, and develop software solutions across multiple projects.\nPerform application testing, identify and resolve systematic and operational issues, and help optimize applications for performance and scalability.\nParticipate in code reviews and contribute to technical documentation.\nCollaborate with principal investigators, contract stakeholders, Application Programmers, Database Analysts, Database Administrators, and Project Managers to address application development, training, and system needs.\nSupport SysOps and DevOps opportunities and complete special projects as requested.\nWhat You’ll Bring\nAdvanced knowledge of Microsoft, open-source, and web-standard technologies.\nUnderstanding of fundamental software design concepts and the Software Development Life Cycle.\nStrong organization and attention to detail.\nEffective written and verbal communication skills.\nAbility to work effectively as part of a multidisciplinary, cross-functional team.\nAdaptability and a collaborative approach to solving technical and stakeholder challenges.\nMinimum Requirements\nBachelor’s degree\n1 year of related experience\nWhat’s In It For You\nOpportunity to develop technology solutions that support state-funded public health initiatives and externally funded projects.\nExperience working across multiple applications and technologies with opportunities to contribute to both SysOps and DevOps activities.\nFully remote eligibility, with approval.\nUK’s Exceptional Benefits\nWhy Now?\nPublic Health Analytics and Informatics supports technology needs connected to state contracts and externally funded projects. This 100% grant-funded position will help the team develop and maintain applications for the DBHDID contract with the State of Kentucky while supporting reliable systems for public health, behavioral health, and intellectual disabilities initiatives.\nBy strengthening application development and maintenance capacity, this role will help investigators and contract stakeholders turn project requirements into dependable, scalable technology solutions.\nSkills / Knowledge / Abilities\nKnowledge of Microsoft, Linux, open-source, and web standard technologies such as ASP . NET Web Forms, ASP . NET MVC , C#, HTML , JavaScript, jQuery, and T- SQL to design and develop technologies.\nDoes this position have supervisory responsibilities? No\nPreferred Education/Experience\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience may substitute and 1 year’s experience in web-based systems object oriented web development using . NET , ASP\nDeadline to Apply 11/06/2026\nOur University Community\nWe value the well-being of each of our employees and are dedicated to creating a healthy place for everyone to work, learn and live. In the interest of maintaining a safe and healthy environment for our students, employees, patients and visitors, the University of Kentucky is a Tobacco & Drug Free campus.\nThe University follows both the federal and state Constitutions as well as all applicable federal and state laws on nondiscrimination. The University provides equal opportunities for qualified persons in all aspects of institutional operations and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnic origin, religion, creed, age, physical or mental disability, veteran status, uniformed service, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, marital status, genetic information or social or economic status.\nAny candidate offered a position may be required to pass pre-employment screenings as mandated by University of Kentucky Human Resources. These screenings may include a national background check and/or drug screen.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483527878": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Objective\nYour role as Software Engineer is to independently design, develop, test, and maintain full-stack software solutions across backend and frontend layers. You will own assigned features from requirement analysis through implementation, integration, QA handover, and production support, while ensuring solutions are reliable, maintainable, secure, and aligned with established engineering standards.\nMain Tasks\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services, APIs, business logic, data processing, frontend applications, dashboards, portals, forms, reporting screens, internal tools, and reusable components.\nOwn assigned features from requirement analysis through development, testing support, QA handover, defect resolution, and production support, with limited supervision.\nImplement complete end-to-end features covering frontend user interactions, backend processing, PostgreSQL data persistence, event queue processing, integrations, and final user or system responses.\nDesign and consume REST APIs, including request and response models, validations, authentication, authorization, error handling, and appropriate integration behavior.\nImplement and maintain integration flows with internal services, operators, aggregators, third-party systems, callbacks, and webhooks, ensuring proper error handling and operational visibility.\nDevelop and validate PostgreSQL queries and database interactions, including transaction behavior, indexing, constraints, data persistence, and consistency requirements for assigned features.\nImplement and support RabbitMQ and event-driven workflows, including event publishing, message consumption, payload validation, retries, dead-letter handling awareness, logging, and queue-processing monitoring.\nImplement and support asynchronous workflows such as notifications, billing triggers, delivery reports, background jobs, audit events, and integration callbacks according to system requirements.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, identify implementation gaps and dependencies, and propose appropriate technical approaches for assigned features before development.\nTroubleshoot and resolve technical issues across backend services, APIs, frontend behavior, PostgreSQL results, event queues, integrations, asynchronous processes, and end-to-end application flows.\nPerform unit testing, support integration and regression testing, resolve identified defects, and validate implemented changes before QA handover and release.\nOptimize standard application performance, including API response times, frontend rendering behavior, PostgreSQL queries, database interactions, and event-processing efficiency.\nCollaborate with QA, Product, DevOps, Support, Security, and other engineering teams to resolve dependencies and ensure smooth end-to-end delivery.\nProvide basic technical guidance to Junior Software Engineers when required and support them in resolving straightforward development and troubleshooting issues.\nEscalate complex architectural, scalability, security, performance, event-driven design, and production-critical concerns to Senior or Lead Software Engineers when required.\nMaintain technical documentation covering APIs, integrations, frontend components, database interactions, event flows, application workflows, configurations, and known technical limitations.\nEnsure development activities comply with Jira traceability, Git and branching practices, pull request and code review requirements, SonarQube validation, secure coding, documentation, and release standards.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n2+ years of experience in software development across backend and frontend applications.\nHands-on experience developing and integrating APIs, databases, and full-stack application features.\nExperience with database-driven applications, event-driven or asynchronous processing, and system integrations.\nExposure to messaging, real-time, high-volume, or integration-heavy platforms is considered an advantage.\nProfessional proficiency in Local Language and English is required.\nGood hands-on knowledge of backend development using Java or C#.NET and frontend development using React and Next.js.\nGood understanding of REST APIs, authentication, authorization, integration patterns, callbacks, webhooks, and error handling.\nGood knowledge of PostgreSQL, SQL queries, transactions, indexing fundamentals, constraints, data persistence, and validation.\nGood understanding of RabbitMQ or similar event-queuing technologies, including producers, consumers, message handling, retries, dead-letter concepts, and asynchronous processing.\nAbility to independently develop and troubleshoot complete features across backend, frontend, database, integration, and event-processing layers.\nGood knowledge of Git workflows, branching strategies, pull requests, code reviews, and development traceability.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483574501": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Work Week: Sunday - Thursday\nWork Timings: Sunday to Thursday, 9:00 AM – 6:00 PM (KSA time)\nAbout Us\nAt Soum, we're on a mission to build a marketplace that enables users to buy and sell anything online with convenience, trust, and ease, starting in the MENA market. We began with second-hand electronics in KSA, becoming market leaders, and are now expanding to used cars and collectibles. In just two years, we've facilitated hundreds of thousands of transactions across 150+ locations in the Kingdom, maintained 10,000 active listings at any given time, earned the distinction of being the 10th most downloaded e-commerce app in KSA for 2023, and received more than 5 million app downloads.\nJob Summary\nWe are seeking a skilled and motivated Backend Software Engineer to join our dynamic team. As a Backend Software Engineer, you will play a critical role in designing, developing, and maintaining scalable backend systems and microservices that power our products.\nIf you have a strong foundation in backend development, enjoy solving complex problems, and thrive in a collaborative environment, we want to hear from you.\nRole & Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend systems using Node.js, TypeScript, and Nest.js.\nBuild and manage scalable microservices architecture with a focus on performance and reliability.\nDevelop APIs and handle inter-service communication using gRPC.\nWork with MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and ClickHouse for data modeling, storage, and optimization.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to understand requirements and deliver high-quality solutions.\nEnsure code quality and maintainability through best practices, code reviews, and testing.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and optimize backend systems to ensure seamless performance.\nRequirements & Qualifications\nRequired Skills\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend systems using Node.js, TypeScript, and Nest.js.\nBuild and manage scalable microservices architecture with a focus on performance and reliability.\nDevelop APIs and handle inter-service communication using gRPC.\nWork with MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and ClickHouse for data modeling, storage, and optimization.\nStrong understanding of CI/CD pipelines and deployment strategies.\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nKnowledge of distributed systems and event-driven architectures.\nQualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n4–5+ years of hands-on experience in backend software development.\nProficient in Node.js and TypeScript.\nExperience working with MongoDB and PostgreSQL in production environments.\nSolid understanding of microservices architecture and communication protocols like gRPC.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills.\nNice to Have\nHands-on experience with Kubernetes and Docker.\nExposure to Golang for building performant backend components.\nExperience in scaling and optimizing backend systems for high-traffic applications.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483649640": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Project Description\nHiredbuddy is looking for an enthusiastic Java Software Engineer to join our remote team. You'll develop, test, and maintain Java-based applications, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and grow your skills in a supportive environment.\nFull Description\nOverview\nHiredbuddy is seeking an entry-level Java Software Engineer to contribute to the design, development, and maintenance of our core software products. This remote role offers an excellent opportunity to work with modern Java technologies, receive mentorship from senior engineers, and build a strong foundation for your career in software development. You will be part of an agile team that values collaboration, continuous learning, and high-quality code.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop, test, and deploy Java-based applications using industry best practices.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code while following coding standards.\nParticipate in code reviews to ensure high-quality deliverables and learn from peer feedback.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams, including product managers, designers, and QA engineers, to understand requirements and implement features.\nDebug and resolve software defects, performing root cause analysis when necessary.\nAssist in the design of RESTful APIs and integrate with front-end components.\nManage database interactions using SQL and ORM frameworks like Hibernate or JPA.\nMaintain and improve existing codebases, refactoring when needed to enhance performance and readability.\nContribute to the creation and maintenance of technical documentation.\nStay updated with emerging trends in Java development and propose improvements to our tech stack.\nQualifications\n0-2 years of professional experience in software development, including internships or personal projects.\nSolid understanding of Java programming language, object-oriented design, and data structures.\nFamiliarity with version control systems, particularly Git.\nBasic knowledge of relational databases and SQL.\nExposure to web development concepts, including REST APIs and HTTP protocols.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nExcellent communication skills, both verbal and written, for remote collaboration.\nA proactive attitude and eagerness to learn new technologies and tools.\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).\nWhy Join Us\nAt Hiredbuddy, we believe in investing in our team's growth. As an entry-level engineer, you will receive dedicated mentorship, access to learning resources, and the opportunity to work on meaningful projects that impact real users. Our remote-first culture promotes work-life balance, flexibility, and autonomy. We celebrate diversity and foster an inclusive environment where everyone's voice is heard.\nIf you are passionate about Java and eager to kick-start your career in a supportive and dynamic team, we'd love to hear from you. Join us in building innovative solutions that make a difference.\nRequirements\n0-2 years of experience in Java development (including academic projects)\nProficiency in Java, OOP principles, and data structures\nBasic understanding of SQL and relational databases\nFamiliarity with Git and version control workflows\nExposure to Spring Framework or similar is a plus\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills\nExcellent communication and teamwork abilities\nWillingness to learn and adapt in a fast-paced environment\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or related field preferred\nBenefits\nPaid time off and holidays\nProfessional development budget for courses and certifications\nCollaborative and inclusive team culture\nAccess to cutting-edge tools and technologies\nRegular team-building activities and virtual events",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484026797": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Overview\nGovCIO is hiring a Frontend Developer to build and modernize federal applications on a serverless AWS GovCloud stack. The developer starts with a focus on frontend work and is expected to grow into a full-stack role.\nThis position is remote within the Continental United States (CONUS).\nJob Description\nA GovCIO Frontend Developer works inside a cross-functional product team with designers, backend developers, DevOps engineers, and test engineers. The developer builds and maintains modern web applications using JavaScript, React, and Redux, integrating them with REST APIs on a serverless AWS backend. Strong skills in JavaScript patterns and practices, frontend frameworks, and CSS/SASS are essential. The role is hands-on and deadline-driven. Work starts and finishes inside the sprint. The developer works from user stories and designer wireframes, builds accessible and secure user interfaces, and understands how the frontend and serverless backend fit together. This Frontend Developer position is expected to grow into a full-stack developer role, building backend services with Python and AWS serverless technologies such as API Gateway, Lambda, and Step Functions. Skills in AWS, Python, and AI coding assistants is essential for this growth.\nResponsibilities\nBuild and maintain React and Redux applications in JavaScript.\nIntegrate frontends with REST APIs on AWS API Gateway and Lambda.\nBuild backend services in Python on AWS serverless technologies as you grow into full-stack work.\nIntegrate AI features built on large language models and vision models into applications, including prompt and context engineering.\nBuild applications that handle non-deterministic AI output, where the same input can produce different valid results.\nBuild pages from designer wireframes using CSS and SASS.\nMeet Section 508 and WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility standards.\nApply frontend security practices, including OWASP guidelines, authentication, JWT handling, and PHI/PII protection.\nMaintain the frontend build chain and keep dependencies current.\nWrite unit and component tests. Build and maintain Cypress end-to-end tests in the CI/CD pipeline.\nSubmit and review GitHub pull requests.\nTake part in sprint planning, backlog refinement, and estimation. Write user stories and tasks in Jira.\nPost daily status updates in Jira.\nSupport UAT, Authority to Operate (ATO), and security compliance activities.\nQualifications\nRequired Skills and Experience\nEducation: Bachelor's degree (required) in computer science, information systems, engineering, mathematics, or a related STEM field, with 5 to 10 years of professional frontend or full-stack development experience. A bachelor's degree in a non-STEM field is acceptable when combined with equivalent professional software engineering experience, technical certifications, or completed technical coursework (such as an accredited bootcamp or graduate certificate).\n5+ years of JavaScript development.\n2+ years of React, including Redux or similar state management.\n2+ years of CSS and SASS.\nExperience integrating frontends with REST APIs on a serverless backend (AWS API Gateway, Lambda).\nPython for backend development.\nFamiliarity with machine learning and AI, especially large language models and vision models.\nAutomated testing experience, including Cypress and Jest or similar.\nGit and GitHub pull request reviews.\nAgile/Scrum experience.\nStrong written and verbal communication skills.\nWilling to earn an AWS Associate certification within the first 9 months.\nClearance : Public Trust.\nPreferred Skills And Experience\nAWS Associate Certification: Architect, Developer, or CloudOps\nML basics: training versus inference, overfitting, and class imbalance.\nGenerative AI fundamentals: tokenization, context windows, hallucination, and temperature.\nNET Core and C# for legacy application maintenance.\nFrontend security: OAuth/OIDC, JWT, Amazon Cognito.\nAWS services such as S3, CloudFront, and CloudWatch.\nBuild tools such as npm, Webpack, or Vite.\nAI coding assistants, especially Claude Code.\nHuman-centered design.\nVA or federal program experience.\nPosted Salary Range: USD $90,000.00 - USD $110,000.00 /Yr.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484040948": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:32:54.966850+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\nWe are looking for a highly skilled Java Developer with strong experience in Spring Boot and Microservices architecture. The ideal candidate will design, develop, and maintain scalable backend services in a cloud-native environment.\nKey Result Areas\n• Design and develop RESTful APIs using Java 8/11/17\n• Build microservices using Spring Boot\n• Implement service-to-service communication (REST, Kafka, etc.)\n• Work with relational and NoSQL databases\n• Write clean, testable, production-grade code\n• Participate in architecture discussions and technical design\n• Implement security using JWT/OAuth2\n• Optimize application performance and scalability\n• Follow CI/CD and DevOps practices\n• Troubleshoot production issues and perform root cause analysis\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n• Strong experience in Java & OOP concepts\n• Hands-on experience with Spring Boot\n• Experience building Microservices architecture\n• Experience with REST APIs\n• Database experience (SQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, MongoDB)\n• Understanding of Docker & Kubernetes\nExperience with Git\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines",
