      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:34:24.257481+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/heykristopher_xbox-is-building-a-new-kind-of-flywheel-with-ugcPost-7513955395246161920-7a3g": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:34:24.257481+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "XBOX is building a new kind of flywheel with games at the center.\n\nThe company announced XP this morning (a clever title)—a new division headed by Kayleen Walters focused on creating more on-ramps for fans to its beloved IP through film & television, consumer products, live events, and strategic partnerships.\n\nHere are the four divisions:\n\n* XBOX PICTURES: Bringing our worlds and characters to new audiences through film, television, and other forms of linear storytelling. \n* XBOX PRODUCTS: Creating products that are authentic to the fandom that allow fans to celebrate and express the franchises they love. \n* XBOX PLACES: Bringing communities together through live events, immersive experiences, attractions, broadcasts, and destinations. \n* XBOX PARTNERSHIPS: Working with creators, brands, and communities to develop new experiences, sponsorships, and brand partnerships.\n\nThe move—championed by Matthew Ball following an internal memo from Asha Sharma—is both elegant and strategic. It adopts the best strategies from Disney and Nintendo, both of whom understand that content is king. Where Disney’s flywheel was built strategically around film and television firs, Nintendo’s is game first.\n\nWith this move, XBOX is positioning itself to move beyond being a mere platform to owning its market position as both a publisher and steward of massive IP (from Minecraft to Halo and beyond).\n\nI’m excited to see where this leads.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-08T13:36:09.005Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moritzbaierlentz_game-studio-funding-is-back-gardens-interactive-share-7513608118791196673-sNWA": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:34:24.257481+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Game studio funding is back: Gardens Interactive has raised a $35M+ Series B, bringing total funding to over $70M before launching its flagship game.\n\nLed by Lightspeed, the round includes Sequoia Capital, Index Ventures, Accel, Eric Schmidt’s Innovation Endeavors, the Nintendo family (Yamauchi No.10), the ZeniMax Media family (James Altman), and the founders of Slack and OpenAI's Sora.\n\nBy any measure, but certainly in 2026, that's an extraordinary vote of confidence and tier-1 syndicate for a pre-launch studio. What inspires that conviction while it seems all venture dollars chase automation?\n\nA team creating a new genre around a simple and proven design principle: deepen human connections, and let the players be the fun.\n\nGardens calls it a “strandbox”: a social roleplaying world where chance encounters become adventures, players shape each other’s stories, and your actions leave something behind for whoever comes next.\n\nFrom serial game-of-the-year creators behind Journey and Sky, the team blends indie creativity and beautiful art with an ambitious AAA live-ops platform bet on how games can create significant and long-lasting emotional encounters.\n\nThis one is deeply personal. I love Stephen, 🔔Chris, and Lexie like brothers. After serving on Gardens’ board for the past three years, I’m rejoining as a personal investor and advisor, doubling down with my own capital and time. To continue an extraordinary development journey that already brought so many wonderful once-strangers together.\n\nI can’t wait for you all to play what they’re building.\n\nBloomberg exclusive by Cecilia D'Anastasio: https://lnkd.in/dYJ4Xj9C",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-07T14:36:12.326Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/the-manila-times_vatican-city-pope-leo-xiv-will-not-attend-activity-7519437751000252418-VFVU": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-29T18:34:24.257481+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "VATICAN CITY — Pope Leo XIV will not attend a peace gathering at Assisi next week on doctors’ advice as he recovers from lung cancer surgery, the Vatican said on Friday.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-23T16:41:04.235Z"
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-10-29T18:34:24.257481+00:00"
  },
